  "$comment": "The stamp catalogue (M31). Data, not code: each entry is drawn by src/engine/appearance/stamp.ts as a rounded box with bold upper-case text in one colour, the generic business-stamp look every PDF editor shares — nothing here is anyone's artwork. `id` is the annotation's /Name; where ISO 32000-1 table 181 names a standard stamp (Approved, Draft, Confidential, Final, ForComment, NotApproved, …) that name is used so other readers recognise it. Lines may carry the tokens {name}, {initials}, {date} and {time}, which make a stamp dynamic. Colours are PDF content colours (RRGGBB), never theme tokens: a stamp keeps its colour whatever theme the reader uses.",
